ort":{"artifact_id":11524653951,"candidate":{"bundle_sha256":"0f4bfa38a44529d32116c03589df9a5f2f98d25473800116858e62c85c84a4ce","changed":true,"changed_paths":["CHANGELOG.md"],"commit":"c8ea549c30ba872fdced76558a347a8ed10edf0f","commits":[{"changed_paths":["CHANGELOG.md"],"commit":"c8ea549c30ba872fdced76558a347a8ed10edf0f","parent":"5f81f28f939a6e697a31f86de9606457dd74d36e","patch_sha256":"d8d5dd6564617f6e762f299ece309281e2f679b6616bc0fc7475049b41c551fe","subject":"Address Copilot review comments: List all removed selector aliases in breaking-change note","tree":"3b56fa1d8a5806763a03f9d0938bf6ecd00fc88b"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"b18105490d4294818a44c1b0120196f0086a10467729f3dc5b464a356b25880b","finding_commits":{"inline:4214073442":"c8ea549c30ba872fdced76558a347a8ed10edf0f","review:5450772447":"c8ea549c30ba872fdced76558a347a8ed10edf0f"},"parent":"5f81f28f939a6e697a31f86de9606457dd74d36e","patch_sha256":"d8d5dd6564617f6e762f299ece309281e2f679b6616bc0fc7475049b41c551fe","tree":"3b56fa1d8a5806763a03f9d0938bf6ecd00fc88b"},"dispositions":{"batches":[{"analysis":"The constructors previously accepted kafka-clients-metrics-0.11, kafka-clients-0.11, kotlinx-coroutines-1.0, kotlinx-coroutines-opentelemetry-instrumentation-annotations and opentelemetry-instrumentation-annotations as aliases; the changelog named only some.","downsides":"Longer changelog entry.","findings":["inline:4214073442","review:5450772447"],"length":1099,"offset":0,"sha256":"d8d5dd6564617f6e762f299ece309281e2f679b6616bc0fc7475049b41c551fe","summary":"List all removed selector aliases in breaking-change note","upsides":"Users with these explicit selectors can find the migration path."}],"findings":[{"analysis":"Overview lists two findings; the changelog one is fixed, the Flow one is not warranted (see inline:4214073404).","disposition":"fixed","downsides":"None significant.","key":"review:5450772447","upsides":"Covers the warranted part."},{"analysis":"Generic @WithSpan instrumentation (opentelemetry-instrumentation-annotations-1.16) is a separate default-enabled module and already instruments Flow-returning methods regardless of the coroutines selector; the Flow module only registers an async end strategy so the span ends on flow completion. Gating it default-off would make Flow spans end at method return, a regression. The PR's selector only governs the suspend-function annotation module, which is what the changelog/README state.","disposition":"not_warranted","downsides":"Flow-returning @WithSpan methods remain traced by default via the generic module.","key":"inline:4214073404","upsides":"Keeps correct Flow span end timing."},{"analysis":"The changelog now lists every removed alias.","disposition":"fixed","downsides":"Longer entry.","key":"inline:4214073442","upsides":"Complete migration guidance."}],"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"74f0515851d4deceaa0f14c8ab0534d0d419db5d67f023593a3fa4c2c6163b61","schema":2},"download_sha256":"ceb1480e1755c5475e8e563ec335b48a3e04c5e72f54db5f8255b9d0e99e6d55","frozen_sha":"5f81f28f939a6e697a31f86de9606457dd74d36e","pr":20428,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"74f0515851d4deceaa0f14c8ab0534d0d419db5d67f023593a3fa4c2c6163b61","request_id":"1694585079b949949797f0d4a79143ce","run_attempt":1,"run_id":37719540375,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:ceb1480e1755c5475e8e563ec335b48a3e04c5e72f54db5f8255b9d0e99e6d55","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":37720664419},"workflow_revision":"934bc4441042ef8eb328caf659fcf03e33d10c33"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5437480319,5437847872,5447139977,5450772447],"budgets":{"deadline_seconds":7200,"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"deadline":1791434769,"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nFlow-returning `@WithSpan` instrumentation remains enabled through the existing Flow module, contradicting the new default.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>2 open findings</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Move Flow instrumentation under the default-off selector](#discussion_r4214073404) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Document all removed public selector aliases](#discussion_r4214073442) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced\n\n---\n\nGive feedback about Copilot approvals in [this survey](https://survey.alchemer.com/s3/9011660/CCR-Public-Preview-Autoapprove-feedback-survey) to enter a drawing for a $150 gift card.","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5450772447","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5450772447},{"body":"[Javaagent] This selector only controls the suspend-function module. `KotlinCoroutinesFlowInstrumentationModule` remains default-enabled under `kotlinx-coroutines` and registers the Flow async-end strategy used by the default-enabled generic `@WithSpan` instrumentation, so methods returning `Flow` still receive full `@WithSpan` instrumentation by default. This contradicts the new documented default and the claim that the broad selector no longer enables annotations. Move the Flow registration under the same default-off selector (and cover the Flow operation in the disabled JVM).","comment_commit_id":"5f81f28f939a6e697a31f86de9606457dd74d36e","comment_id":4214073404,"key":"inline:4214073404","kind":"inline","line":22,"original_commit_id":"5f81f28f939a6e697a31f86de9606457dd74d36e","original_line":22,"path":"instrumentation/kotlinx-coroutines/kotlinx-coroutines-1.0/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/kotlinxcoroutines/v1_0/instrumentationannotations/AnnotationInstrumentationModule.java","review_commit_id":"5f81f28f939a6e697a31f86de9606457dd74d36e","review_id":5450772447,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-08T02:44:33Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"887093ed75b27decded34249f1c104baa7ad989ec814db8fed98e8bbbdd09f80","id":4214073404,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-08T02:44:33Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86qLGki"},{"body":"[Config] This breaking-change note omits several removed public selectors from the constructors. Users who run with global instrumentation disabled and explicitly enable `kafka-clients-metrics-0.11`, `kafka-clients-0.11`, `kotlinx-coroutines-1.0`, `kotlinx-coroutines-opentelemetry-instrumentation-annotations`, or `opentelemetry-instrumentation-annotations` are also affected, but the migration note currently does not identify those configurations. List every removed alias so those users can migrate to the dedicated selectors.","comment_commit_id":"5f81f28f939a6e697a31f86de9606457dd74d36e","comment_id":4214073442,"key":"inline:4214073442","kind":"inline","line":11,"original_commit_id":"5f81f28f